competitors in the race, this bunch are out to settle personal scores - or perhaps just enjoy the sunshine. The runners are: Financial wizards Keith Miller (106) and Jim Heathfield (93), Ted Pallant (94), talented youth and junior Tony Brooks (37) - lost to the sport before making impact as a senior, Dave McMillan (12) - now fighting back from terrible injuries sustained while out training and hit by a car, P.Blair-Fish (46).","id":"B225-16","w":"February 1997"},{"f":"crops/B227/B227-p29-battersea-880-c1955.jpg","c":"Above: Chas (18) tears into the lead on the first lap of a Club Championship 880 yards Race at Battersea Park. We are not absolutely certain of the year but it was probably 1955, one of the years when Charlie Walker, (4) at the back of the pack became Club Champion over the distance. Behind Charlie Manning can be seen a youthful Jim Heathfield. Can anyone put names to the other faces in the picture?","id":"B227-62","w":"March 1999"},{"f":"crops/B221/B221-p09-young-athletes-1970s.jpg","c":"Above: The 70s and a photo call after a Young Athletes Sunday morning training session at Wimbledon Park. The adults, left of the group, left to right are: John Martin, Frank Simmons, Jim Heathfield (crouching), Bob Taylor, Reg. Hopkins Jnr., Reg Hopkins Snr. And on the right: John Baker, Philip Gee, Peter Hilliar, Gordon Biscoe, Mickey Pyer, Gordon Doubleday, Alan Mead and Bill Couzens.","id":"B221-23","w":"Winter 1993/94"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B217/B217-p29-heathfield-biscoe-davies.jpg","caption":"Jim Heathfield and Gordon Biscoe get a quote for \"The Belgravian\" from sage John Davies.","source":"B217-105","when":"December 1991"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Jim Heathfield in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1960–1999: 96 mentions in 52 issues, 70 race results and 4 photographs. Wrote or reported 1 item.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B217/B217-p29-heathfield-biscoe-davies.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1